{"item_id":"E-RES-627","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Turn the abstract topic into a bounded Bareni workflow decision."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI fits"}],"rationale":"This is a planning instruction to reframe the owner-specified abstract topic into a single recurring workflow decision; it asserts no current Bareni capability or customer use. The framing of one recurring workflow and human control points matches the approved diagnostic model and the mandatory human-approval boundary.","use_guidance":"Keep as an explicit framing proposal. Present the three maintenance options as an illustrative decision framework for the reader's own business, not as an option set Bareni has implemented or observed in customer work. Retain human control points (C04: human approval mandatory for high-risk decisions)."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a
  measurable outcome"}],"rationale":"A diagnostic question and a request to name one measurable outcome are permissible instructions, not factual assertions. The persona focus explicitly authorises one diagnostic question, and approved evidence describes a measurable outcome as a fit criterion.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly as a diagnostic question the reader answers for themselves. Do not attach any figure, benchmark or hours-saved number to either option, and do not imply Bareni has measured such costs (C05: numbers require source and status)."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Human approval is mandatory for money movement and other high-risk decisions."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"general document, email, CRM, and back-office
  workflows using AI plus Zapier, Make, n8n, and small amounts of custom code"},{"source_id":"C03","quote":"amount-based human-only approval,
  refusal of agent approval/payment attempts, and persistent audit records work"}],"rationale":"The fit condition and the human go/no-go boundary are consistent with approved evidence, but the wording "AI can systematise logging and sequencing" reads as a general current capability statement for maintenance workflows. Approved evidence covers document, email, CRM and back-office automation plus three self-built demos; maintenance runbook or rollback automation is not among the demonstrated systems.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that this is a general fit criterion, and phrase any automation as what a scoped pilot could be designed to do within document, email, CRM and back-office workflow tooling — not as an existing Bareni maintenance capability. Keep the owner's go/no-go and any high-risk step under human approval; no autonomous action."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Normal sequence: free 30-minute diagnostic; free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI
  fits, and—if it does—defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures."}],"rationale":"The diagnostic-then-pilot-scope structure is directly supported, and excluding autonomous deployment respects the human-approval boundary. However the claim omits that the diagnostic is free and 30 minutes, that the pilot also carries a fixed price and measures, and it presents alert consolidation, pre-flight checklists and incident reporting without marking them as hypothetical examples rather than existing Bareni offerings.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that the diagnostic is a free 30-minute conversation and that a pilot, if it fits, comes with defined scope, fixed price and measures presented as intended scope rather than a guarantee. Label the three automation ideas explicitly as examples of possible pilot boundaries, not delivered work."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Informational posts use no CTA or one soft closing sentence."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"free 30-minute diagnostic"}],"rationale":"This is a proposed next-step sentence in founder voice, not a factual assertion about outcomes; the balanced "saves hours or just adds complexity" avoids promising a result. But the task sets CTA rule: None, so the sentence must not function as a booking call to action.","use_guidance":"Keep as a proposal only if rewritten as a soft, non-CTA closing observation about clarifying fit; remove any invitation phrasing that acts as "Book a free 30-minute diagnostic". Do not state or imply an hours-saved figure (C05)."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work;
  bulk cold-email automation; scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows; and requests
  that require unsupported compliance or security guarantees."},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Present these as
  current scope discipline, not claims that the work can never be automated."}],"rationale":"Declining work that requires unsupported compliance or security guarantees is supported, but the claim's second half, "most operational small-business windows are not", is an unsupported generalisation about the market, and the exclusion is stated without marking it as current scope discipline.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that these exclusions are Bareni's current scope discipline, not a statement that such work can never be automated. Drop or rewrite the "most ... are not" generalisation, since no approved evidence characterises the prevalence of small-business maintenance windows. Also avoid any legal characterisation or advice (C04)."}]}

